        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cac43de8-2a58-5629-87af-68630f053934",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Cepello, Jesse Ventura, Mark Dayton, Steve Strong, Steve Barkley\n- Places: Minnesota, Governor's Mansion, Minnesota State Capitol, Monterey\n- Roles: Governor of Minnesota, wrestler, artist, comic\n- Works: Elephant Parts, Rio, Cruisin'\n- Topics: portrait painting, retirement from wrestling, comedy sketches, music videos\n\nFacts:\n- After retiring from wrestling to focus on his art career, Stephen Cepello was selected to paint the official Governor's Mansion and Minnesota State Capitol portraits of former wrestler and Governor of Minnesota Jesse Ventura.\n- \"Elephant Parts\" is one hour long and includes parody commercials, comedy sketches, and five full-length music videos.\n- In \"Elephant Parts,\" the popular songs \"Rio\" and \"Cruisin'\" are featured among the music videos.\n- The song \"Cruisin'\" in \"Elephant Parts\" featured wrestler Steve Strong and Monterey-based comic Steve Barkley.\n- Mark Dayton of the Democratic-Farmer-Labor Party is the current governor of Minnesota.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
